## Known v0.1 issues (must fix before v0.2)

1. `transforms/numbers.ts::obfuscateNumbers` does NOT actually mutate the
   token stream usefully — the pipeline redoes D2 on the AST instead.
   Either delete the function or rewire it to consume the same RNG state
   as the pipeline (so seeded output is reproducible either way).
2. `src/transforms/identifier.ts::buildMapping` only emits single-char
   names; for >53 names it produces a 2-char scheme that uses positions
   `0..25` and `0..51` and may collide. Replace with an
   injectively-mapped scheme (e.g. base-52 with explicit skipping).
3. `parse()` does NOT round-trip — e.g. hex literals are kept as raw
   strings; `(function ...) end` with a table-string call arg may emit
   wrong. The emitter assumes the AST was in canonical form. Verify with
   obfuscate→luau-cli for `examples/hello.lua` before expanding scope.
4. The emit `'__STR__'` synthetic token in
   `transforms/strings.ts::obfuscateStrings` is dead code — the pipeline
   walks the AST and never sees the token. Safe to delete.

