## How to verify v0.1 actually runs

```bash
npm install
npm test
```

If `npm install` fails because of network restrictions, the build still
works for users with access (the source does not depend on anything
beyond commander + vitest). For your local testing on this workspace you
may need:

```bash
npm install --no-audit --prefer-offline
```

If you have access to a luau interpreter (luau-cli, the Roblox Studio
console, or a custom npm-wrapped version), drop the obfuscated output
into a `print()` and confirm it produces the same output as the original
source. If you don't, rely on `tests/roundtrip.test.ts` to confirm
cipher identity.

